                <pb facs="0711" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./584:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-02T12:00:00-05:00">August 2,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. Your 90, August 1, 6 p.m. When the statements first appeared in the
                    newspapers I objected both orally and in an informal letter to the Foreign
                    Minister. Subsequent articles which were prepared have not appeared in the
                    press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
